From 9ee5e670758305725265cc26e17b81c020b02b92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xz-dev <xiangzhedev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gud: preserve TV mode slot bounds for FORTIFY

Commit da1ea35fea67 ("drm/gud: validate TV mode names before creating
enum property") validates each fixed-size TV mode name with memchr().

The receive buffer is represented as char *, so Clang loses the size of
each fixed-size slot. The returned byte count is also not explicitly
bounded by the allocated buffer. With Clang 23, -O3 and
CONFIG_FORTIFY_SOURCE, the inlined memchr() is therefore rejected as a
read beyond the object.

Represent the buffer as an array of protocol-sized slots and validate the
returned byte count before indexing it. This gives FORTIFY both bounds
needed to prove that each fixed-size scan stays within the allocation.

Fixes: da1ea35fea67 ("drm/gud: validate TV mode names before creating enum property")
Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/da1ea35fea67ad841f4ada28dd61b41be65e5437
Signed-off-by: xz-dev <xiangzhedev@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -379 +379,2 @@
-	size_t buf_len = GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN;
+	char (*buf)[GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];
+	size_t buf_len = GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM * sizeof(*buf);
@@ -382 +382,0 @@
-	char *buf;
@@ -393 +393 @@
-	if (!ret || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
+	if (!ret || ret > buf_len || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
@@ -400,3 +400,3 @@
-		char *mode = &buf[i * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];
-
-		if (!memchr(mode, '\0', GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN)) {
+		char *mode = buf[i];
+
+		if (!memchr(mode, '\0', sizeof(*buf))) {
